IMPORT prelude

-- Pensions (Expatriate Officers) Act (Singapore, Cap. 226) -- who is an "officer" (s 2), what is a "law relating to pensions"
-- (s 2), and when that law ceases to apply to an officer, his widow, child or legal personal representative (s 3). That is the
-- whole operative Act: s 1 is the short title.
--
-- Edition: 1985 Revised Edition (Chapter 226), informal consolidation "version in force from 30/3/1987", as deposited at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/PEOA1976.txt. Original enactment Act 17 of 1976, commenced 1 October 1976. The legislative history
-- in the deposit lists no amendment after the 1985 Revised Edition (date of operation 30 March 1987).
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement REQ-0197 in subjects/sg/requirements.jsonl: Tier 3 of the remaining Singapore Acts, ordered by
-- everyday-life relevance. The requirement asks what the Act decides for a person it applies to; no scenario has asked a sharper
-- question yet. The Act is three sections long, so the whole of it is encoded.
--
-- Not encoded: the Public Officers' Pension (Singapore) Agreement 1976 and the 1964 Public Officers Agreement themselves (neither is
-- in the deposit), so "the 1964 Agreement applies or applied to him" and "the UK has assumed responsibility for his pension" are
-- taken as given facts; what pension the United Kingdom pays; and the content of the three disapplied laws. Dates are written as
-- YYYYMMDD numbers.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules conventions of the example rows. No pipeline, no
-- coverage table, no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Pensions (Expatriate Officers) Act`

§§ `2 -- "officer"`

-- s 2: "officer" means an officer "to whom the Public Officers Agreement ... signed at Kuala Lumpur on 9th July 1964 applies or
-- applied and who was not a citizen of Singapore on 1st April 1971 or who, having retired from the public service or having died in
-- public service after that date, is not or was not a citizen of Singapore at the time of his retirement or death, as the case may
-- be."
--
-- Read as two limbs joined by "or". Limb 1 looks only at 1 April 1971, so a non-citizen on that day who later became a citizen is
-- still an "officer". Limb 2 catches a citizen of 1 April 1971 who retired or died in service AFTER that date and was not a citizen
-- at that time. "After that date" is read strictly: retirement on 1 April 1971 itself is not after it.
GIVEN `the 1964 Agreement applies or applied to him` IS A BOOLEAN
      `citizen on 1 April 1971` IS A BOOLEAN
      `retired or died in service` IS A BOOLEAN
      `date of retirement or death` IS A NUMBER
      `citizen at retirement or death` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `he is an officer under s 2` IF
        `the 1964 Agreement applies or applied to him`
    AND (    (NOT `citizen on 1 April 1971`)
         OR  (    `retired or died in service`
              AND `date of retirement or death` GREATER THAN 19710401
              AND (NOT `citizen at retirement or death`)))

§§ `2 -- "law relating to pensions"`

-- s 2: "law relating to pensions" means (a) "the Retirement from the Public Service (Compensation) Ordinance 1956"; (b) "the Pensions
-- Act [Cap. 225] and the regulations made thereunder"; and (c) "the Widows' and Orphans' Pension Act [Cap. 350]". The list is closed
-- ("means"). The Central Provident Fund Act is added below only as a law the definition does NOT name.
DECLARE Law IS ONE OF
    `the Retirement from the Public Service (Compensation) Ordinance 1956`
    `the Pensions Act or regulations under it`
    `the Widows' and Orphans' Pension Act`
    `the Central Provident Fund Act`

GIVEN `the law` IS A Law
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `it is a law relating to pensions` IF
    CONSIDER `the law`
    WHEN `the Central Provident Fund Act` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `3 -- the law relating to pensions ceases to apply`

-- s 3: "With effect from 1st January 1978, the law relating to pensions shall cease to apply to any officer or to his widow or child
-- or to his legal personal representative in respect of whom the Government of the United Kingdom ... has assumed responsibility
-- for the payment of pension in accordance with the provisions of the Agreement." Footnote: 1 January 1978 is "The appointed day for
-- the purpose of the Agreement, as mutually arranged" between the two Governments.
--
-- The Act commenced on 1 October 1976, but nothing ceases until 1 January 1978. Only the four named kinds of person are covered;
-- any other dependant (a parent, say) is not. "In respect of whom" is read as attaching to the person claiming: the UK must have
-- assumed responsibility for the pension in that person's case (an inference -- the text could be read as attaching to the officer
-- alone). Whether "widow" extends to a widower is not decided by this text; it is not encoded.
DECLARE Claimant IS ONE OF
    `the officer himself`
    `his widow`
    `his child`
    `his legal personal representative`
    `another dependant`

GIVEN `the claimant` IS A Claimant
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 3 reaches the claimant` IF
    CONSIDER `the claimant`
    WHEN `another dependant` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `the law` IS A Law
      `the claimant` IS A Claimant
      `the person is an officer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the UK assumed responsibility for the pension` IS A BOOLEAN
      `on date` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 3 disapplies the law` IF
        `it is a law relating to pensions` `the law`
    AND `s 3 reaches the claimant` `the claimant`
    AND `the person is an officer`
    AND `the UK assumed responsibility for the pension`
    AND `on date` AT LEAST 19780101

-- The same answer read the other way round, for a claimant who asks whether the Singapore law still governs his pension. It is
-- "still applies" only in the sense that THIS Act does not switch it off; the Act says nothing about whether the law otherwise
-- covers the claimant.
GIVEN `the law` IS A Law
      `the claimant` IS A Claimant
      `the person is an officer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the UK assumed responsibility for the pension` IS A BOOLEAN
      `on date` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `this Act leaves the law in place` IF
    NOT (`s 3 disapplies the law` `the law` `the claimant` `the person is an officer` `the UK assumed responsibility for the pension` `on date`)
